WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:07.520
Okay, so Inuzuka-sensei is out today...

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.180
Free period? Yes!

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:10.280
Nope!

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.120
Handouts?

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.960
He said if you can understand this, 
your final should be easy.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.490
Did he tell us yesterday that he'd be out today?

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.600
I don't remember.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.640
Think something might've happened?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.090
<b>Illness</b>

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.090
<b>Accident</b>

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.090
<b>Trouble</b>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.090
<b>Did something happen
to Tsumugi-chan?</b>

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.430
Y-You're so bold about eating in class...

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:46.560
Okay, today is the day we 
bring our families to school!

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.020
Let's all do morning greetings together!

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.150
Okay!

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>Squid and Taro Stew That's Still Yummy Tomorrow</b>

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.650
Wait! Hey!

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.930
Sensei, I see you made it today!

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.360
Yes, I took just the morning off.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.560
I'm heading back as soon as we're done.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.790
You're so busy!

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.650
First we see how they usually 
spend their mornings...

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.880
And then we join them in a game?

00:02:58.880 --> 00:02:59.980
Mommy!

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.680
You wanna see this?

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.280
Want me to show it to you?

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.330
Oh? Let me see.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.690
Come on, show me!

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.210
What are you making, Tsumugi?

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:11.960
A squid!

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:13.880
A squid?

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.570
Yup!

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:19.380
It's hard to make 'cause it's so big!

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.880
Today I'm sticking this to this,

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.570
and taking this part off to redo it!

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.850
That's very good, Tsumugi-chan!

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.230
Really?

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.290
Which part is good?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.540
Where?

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.940
Um... It's so big and bold!

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.760
I like how big it is!

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.240
Isn't that great, Tsumugi-chan?

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.270
Yuuka-chan's mommy is good at handicrafts, 
so if she says so, it means something.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.010
Yeah!

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.570
I'm not really...

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.500
Sure you are.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.370
Your bags and purses look 
like store merchandise!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.720
That's so pretty!

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.330
If you have a daughter, you like to be 
able to do things like that for her.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:57.420
Yup, yup!

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.360
It's so nice to have a talent for that.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.550
The one you made this year was cute, too.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.800
I'm on my third son,

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.700
so I'm just going to keep using 
that bag until it breaks.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.030
It's pretty hard to make a 
new one every year, isn't it?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.920
I've got two kids to make them for.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:13.940
Um...

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.440
Do you make your bags every year?

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:26.590
Well, there are a few households that 
remake them every year, just because.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.900
Yes. It's not a rule or anything.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.000
I just bought mine at a store.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.790
I still use the one from 
when mine were younger.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.480
Don't let it bother you.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.510
Right...

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.990
That's right!

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.300
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.300
<b>Inuzuka Tsumugi</b>

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.850
Okay, everyone!

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.110
We're going to play a game with your families!

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.940
Once you've cleaned up, 
let's go to the bathroom.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.170
Okay!

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.450
Oh, a game!

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.270
Next is the game, huh?

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.400
Thank you!

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.470
Sure.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:19.420
Um, Iida-san?

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.540
Can I help you?

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.880
I-It's nothing!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.440
Excuse me!

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.100
I can't ask her about Sensei...

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.860
Now I'll explain how to play the game.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:41.860
<b>Telephone Game</b>

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.420
What's wrong, Mikio-kun?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.200
I gotta poopies.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.200
He said "poopies"!

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.660
You should've gone earlier!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.580
Are you okay, Mikio-kun?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.050
Oh, it's fine, it's fine.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.960
Just start without us.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.190
Aww!

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.300
Don't worry!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.510
I'll wait for your poopies!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.280
It's okay, Tsumugi-chan.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.750
You can start without us.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:12.300
But we don't get to have 
our parents here very often.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:17.590
There are never this many people here, right?

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:19.650
I'll wait while you poopies!

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.520
I'll wait, too.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.650
Yeah, I'll wait!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.040
I'll wait, too!

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.660
Me, too!

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.110
And me!

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.680
Okay, let's chat while we wait.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.440
Mikio-kun, no need to hurry, okay?

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.250
Okay!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.880
<b>Telephone Game</b>

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.590
Teacher likes curry.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.930
Know what?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.350
Teacher went poopies!

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.380
Mikio-kun's not funny!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.620
You're not funny!

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:19.250
That was so funny!

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.290
No, it wasn't funny!

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.750
There, there...

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.720
You just wanted to get everybody 
laughing again, didn't you?

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.300
Okay, let's all say the right answer.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.970
Ready?

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.220
Teacher likes curry!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.420
Tsumugi?

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.380
Did you have fun today?

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:57.290
Yeah!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.660
It was fun!

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.540
After you left,

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:06.010
Mikio-kun said when we grow up, he'll marry me.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.140
Want me to marry you?

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.700
A-And then?

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.260
And then I said...

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.530
"Nwope."  Like that.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:23.020
Mikio-kun's a meanie, you know.

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.720
I see!

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.120
Poor Mikio-kun!

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.950
Daddy, can I watch <i>Magi-Girl</i> before bed?

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:34.420
Sure.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:37.120
<b>Inuzuka Tsumugi</b>

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.530
Hey, Tsumugi.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.000
I'm thinking of making a new bag for you.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:53.890
Why?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:59.100
A lot of the girls are getting new bags 
now that they're a little older, right?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.270
There's a stain here that won't 
come out when I wash it.

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:16.490
It's fine.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.790
I want Mommy's.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.220
I see.

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.580
That's right.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.660
You can take good care of Mommy's bag,

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:41.420
but Daddy wants to do something for you!

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.940
If there's anything Mommy made 
that you want to eat again,

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.070
I'll make it for you.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.610
Anything.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:01.740
Squid!

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.620
Squid?

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.290
Squid and yams!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.580
The stew!

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.250
Squid?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.620
That one?!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.300
Um, Sensei, what happened yesterday?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:25.040
Oh, it was Parents' Day at Tsumugi's school,

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.480
so I took the morning off.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.810
Parents' Day?

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:32.190
So that was why.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.110
<b>Barley Tea
Zero Caffeine</b>

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.110
Squid and taro stew?

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.180
That's a pretty mature request.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:44.030
Yes, it was so sudden that I couldn't remember 
what she was talking about at first.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:49.610
Something Tsumugi-chan wants to eat again...

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:56.240
Is there anything like an 
Inuzuka family recipe?

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.460
I'm sorry, there isn't.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:01.970
I see.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.100
I'll ask my mom.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:08.140
The recipe will be pretty basic, but...

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.240
Great!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.140
Thank you!

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.060
Squid! Squid!

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.170
Want some clay?

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.290
Nope!

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.520
'Kay...

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:27.520
Squid!

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.420
So today...

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:43.930
Squid! Squid! Squid! Squid!

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:43.930
We're going to make squid and taro stew!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.860
This was my request,

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:48.060
so work really hard!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.980
Okay!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.690
Squid? Squid. Squid!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.700
I had her write out a really basic recipe,

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.630
so it shouldn't taste completely different, but...

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.480
You put okra in, huh?

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:07.200
We use it to add color.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.640
Is that okay?

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.660
It shouldn't change the flavor.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:16.840
Squid! Squid! Squid! Squid!

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:18.280
I'm sorry if it's not the flavor 
Tsumugi-chan was hoping for.

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:21.180
No, it's fine!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.970
That's not what I meant...

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.640
You don't have to perfectly 
recreate how we used to eat it.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.760
I'm sorry.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.690
This is putting a lot of pressure on you, huh?

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:35.860
It's okay.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.980
First, I want to be able to make the basic dish.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.450
Please tell me what I have to do to make it good.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.240
Okay!

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:50.460
First, let's do something about the squid.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.080
Right.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:57.190
First, put your fingers into the body.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:58.500
Um...

00:12:58.950 --> 00:12:59.740
Here?

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:01.960
Like this?

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.660
I'm okay.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.930
Yeah...

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.890
Pull it out quick,

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.280
so that the insides don't get damaged.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:17.650
Okay.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:26.800
Want to try it, Tsumugi?

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:27.410
Huh?

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:30.380
O-Okay...

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:45.640
Sorry.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.340
I was acting kind of weird.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.920
I'm glad you're back to normal.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:56.620
Now cut the washed squid into 
round slices, with the skin still on.

00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:57.350
Okay.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.810
Separate the tentacles and the 
insides right under the eyes.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:13.220
And take off the beak that's still in the legs.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.410
I see something that looks like a fang.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.300
This is it, right?

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.670
The suckers are...

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.170
The firm parts.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.800
Rub them off with your hands.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:44.900
Tsumugi?

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.920
I was this close to an epiphany.

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:55.490
Sorry, sorry!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.370
Look, I'm about to stew the squid. 
I thought you'd like to watch.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.830
Put the torso in first.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.930
Once it starts boiling, add the tentacles,

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.350
then take it out after about a minute.

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.040
Okay.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.450
I've seen that before.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.140
Now the taro.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.290
They look small and hard to peel,

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:48.610
but supposedly it's better to 
cut the skin off in thick slices.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:50.230
Good luck!

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.440
I see.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:53.930
So it's better to use a knife than a peeler.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:58.140
First, cut off the top and bottom.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:05.010
Then peel the surface from top to bottom.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:05.770
Okay.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.400
It's slimy and hard to hold,

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.950
but as long as I don't have to peel it thin...

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.250
Daddy, did you cut your finger?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.190
Nope.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.890
T-Tell me when you're done.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.140
It's okay!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.580
Daddy's getting better!

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.610
Yeah.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.660
Thanks!

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:56.740
It's okay!

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.410
I'm done.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:05.960
Okay!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.510
Once you add the taro,

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:10.960
put on the lid and stew for about 20 minutes.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.840
And while we wait, let's make miso soup!

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:16.550
Okay.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.480
We'll make a light soup,

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.060
with green onions and tofu.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.280
I'll cut them.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.520
Then we get the okra ready...

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:25.130
The gas rice cooker!

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.340
We're making today's rice in a gas cooker.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.020
<b>Just Washed</b>

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.020
<b>Left to Soak</b>

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.020
<b>Keep Warm</b>

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.020
<b>Off</b>

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.020
<b>Cook</b>

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.680
I'll help, too!

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:33.780
Then can you help me get the okra ready?

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:35.800
Okay!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:40.700
So you roll them like this,

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.520
to rub in the salt.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:46.620
Um...

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.410
Like this?

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:51.510
That's right.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:55.590
I realized this when I was making lunches,

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:58.440
but when you're making lots of side dishes,

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.550
you need to plan, don't you?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.170
That's right.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:04.750
You need to be able to take advantage

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.160
of your down time to do other things.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.580
Salty!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:13.020
Is it just about done?

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:15.440
The taro are soft all the way through.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.780
And it tastes fine!

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:21.210
Now we just add the okra.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.660
And once it's boiling again,

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.510
add the squid,

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:30.300
mix, and...

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.010
It's done!

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.340
Let's eat!

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.790
Is it good, Tsumugi-chan?

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:01.980
Yup!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.480
I'm so glad...

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.570
It's so good!

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:14.980
The squid and taro are so soft!

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.260
What's this?

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.310
A crown?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:31.380
Oh, that's where the squid's arms connect.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:32.860
Is it like a crown?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.730
Squid are so cool!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.040
I didn't know they had these!

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:41.650
Next time, put this in, Daddy!

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:42.860
I see.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.220
You like it, huh?

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.150
Yup!

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.920
I'll eat the crown last!

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:55.110
I wonder if stews taste the same 
in every household.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:58.240
No, I don't know about that.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.920
Some use a lighter taste.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.530
Some add ginger.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.450
I think people make it lots of ways.

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:05.860
I see...

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.610
It's strange.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:12.730
I've never made this before,

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.560
but it feels like I've had it many times.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:19.060
Tsumugi,

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.430
is Daddy's good, too?

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:23.480
Yup!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.700
It's the taste I love!

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:27.680
I'm glad.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.040
I'll make it again, okay?

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:40.960
Thank you.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.600
Sensei, wait.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:46.840
Here you go.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:51.260
We can have the leftovers?

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:54.190
I made a little extra so you could.

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:58.150
Once stews get cold, the flavor soaks in.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.150
So it'll be even better tomorrow.

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:03.340
Tomorrow?

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:05.280
It'll be better tomorrow?

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:07.030
Wow!

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:11.830
I can't wait!

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:13.060
Great!

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.230
Tsumugi,

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.850
want me to put a cute patch

00:21:21.850 --> 00:21:24.550
over the stain on your bag?

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:31.560
Can Daddy participate in what Mommy made?

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:35.560
Let's go to the crafts store tomorrow.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.340
I can't wait 'til tomorrow!

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.000
Look! Look at this!

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:50.440
It's so cute!

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.040
What a cute apple!

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:53.920
Yup!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:56.000
Daddy and Mommy made it together!
